<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center; background-color: white"><FONT STYLE="background-color: white"><B>EXPLANATORY
NOTE</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center; background-color: white">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; background-color: white"><FONT STYLE="background-color: white">E-Home
Household Service Holdings Limited </FONT>(the &ldquo;<B>Company</B>&rdquo;) held an extraordinary general meeting of the Company at 10:00
a.m. on May 1, 2025, local time, at E-Home, 18/F, East Tower, Building B, Dongbai Center, Yangqiao Road, Gulou District, Fuzhou City 350001,
China (the &ldquo;<B>Meeting</B>&rdquo;). At the Meeting, shareholders of the Company approved a share consolidation of the Company&rsquo;s
issued and unissued ordinary shares of the Company (the &ldquo;<B>Ordinary Shares</B>&rdquo;) at a ratio of not less than one (1)-for-two
(2) and not more than one (1)-for-fifty (50) (the &ldquo;<B>Range</B>&rdquo;), with the exact ratio to be set at a whole number within
this Range to be determined by the Board of the Directors of the Company (the &ldquo;<B>Board</B>&rdquo;) in its sole discretion within
180 calendar days after the date of passing of these resolutions (the &ldquo;<B>Share Consolidation</B>&rdquo;). At the Meeting, the shareholders
of the Company also approved and authorized the Board to round up any fractions of Ordinary Shares issued to or registered in the name
of such shareholders of the Company in respect of any fractional entitlements to the issued consolidated shares resulting from the Share
Consolidation, if so determined by the Board in its sole discretion.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; background-color: white">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; background-color: white">The Board reserves its
right to determine not to proceed with, and abandon, the Share Consolidation contemplated above if it determines in its sole discretion
that implementing the Share Consolidation is not in the best interests of the Company and its shareholders. As such, if the Board did
not determine a ratio within such 180-day period, the Share Consolidation would not proceed and will be abandoned.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; background-color: white">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; background-color: white"><FONT STYLE="background-color: white"></FONT></P>

